<title>SOUTH KOREA: Sewon hits limit up on Miwon merger bid.</title>
<headline>Sewon hits limit up on Miwon merger bid.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Sewon Co went limit up in Friday's early morning trading as Miwon Co began buying Sewon shares to merge the two companies, brokers said.</p>
<p>Sewon gained 5,200 won or 7.9 percent to 84,700 in early trading but later fell to 80,000.  </p>
<p>Miwon said it began purchases of 210,000 common shares of Sewon on Thursday. Sewon was spun off from Miwon in 1994.</p>
<p>A Miwon official said when completed, the purchases will bring the firm's stake in Sewon to 9.94 percent from the current 2.2 percent.</p>
<p>Miwon is South Korea's leading food processing company and Sewon is the largest corn processing firm.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
